{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Then we turned and journeyed into the wilderness.</b> Had they not sinned, they would have passed by way of Mount Seir to enter the Land from its south to its north. But because they corrupted, they turned toward the wilderness side — which is between the Sea of Reeds and the south of Mount Seir — and traveled along its south, from west to east. <b>By the way of the Sea of Reeds.</b> The route of their departure from Egypt, which is at the southwestern corner; from there they would travel toward the east." "<b>And we circled Mount Seir.</b> The entire south side, as far as the land of Moab."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:37.130961669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}